$ zenctl snapshot diff --help
Compare two .zsnap files, offline.

No bus. Both spans are stated, the facets (value, verdict, registration, holder) stay apart, and an origin an alignment could not pair is listed, never dropped. Exit 0 identical, 1 they differ, 2 a file could not be read.

Usage: zenctl snapshot diff [OPTIONS] <A> <B>

Arguments:
  <A>
          The earlier snapshot

  <B>
          The later snapshot

Options:
      --normalize-origins
          Align origins across deployments — by the `source` label their health/sensor documents carry, then by producer set — and roll the diff up per subject. Refuses (exit 2) over any origin it cannot pair, and lists them

      --map <A=B>
          An explicit origin pairing, `A=B` (a's origin = b's), repeatable; decided before any automatic pairing. Requires --normalize-origins

      --max-changes <N>
          Field-level changes listed per key before the rest are counted
          
          [default: 20]

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format: table for humans, json (one document) or ndjson (one object per row) for scripts; auto = table on a tty, ndjson piped
          
          [env: ZENCTL_FORMAT=]
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, table, json, ndjson]

      --color <COLOR>
          Colour: auto (a terminal gets it, a pipe does not), always, never.
          
